import SocialAgentPage from "../../components/SocialAgentPage.astro";
---

<SocialAgentPage
  current="privacy"
  title="Social Agent privacy"
  lead="How this privately operated tool accesses, uses, stores, and handles Google user data."
  description="Privacy notice for Social Agent, including its read-only Google access, data use, storage, retention, and deletion process."
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 5, 2026.</p>

  <p>
    Social Agent is operated by Shariq Hirani for private content publishing and
    growth reporting. This notice covers Google user data accessed through the
    Social Agent integration. It does not turn the private dashboard into a
    public service.
  </p>

  <h2>Google data the tool accesses</h2>

  <p>Social Agent requests these Google OAuth scopes:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>webmasters.readonly</code> for authorized Search Console property, page,
      date, and query performance.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>youtube.readonly</code> for authorized YouTube channel and video metadata.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>yt-analytics.readonly</code> for aggregate viewing and engagement statistics,
      such as views, engaged views, watch time, and average view duration.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    These grants are read-only. They do not provide the Google account password
    or permission to upload, edit, or delete videos. Search Console query
    results can be provider-limited rather than exhaustive, and the reports
    preserve that limitation instead of treating missing data as a measured
    zero.
  </p>

  <h2>How Google data is used</h2>

  <p>
    The tool links the operator's published content with private search and
    viewing reports so the operator can understand available evidence and decide
    what to improve. The data is not sold, shared with data brokers, used for
    advertising, or used to build advertising profiles.
  </p>

  <p>
    Growth reports are generated deterministically and do not require sending
    Google API data to a third-party language model. Separate content-drafting
    workflows may use a model to prepare drafts, but they are not the Google
    reporting flow and remain subject to human approval before publication.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage and access</h2>

  <p>
    Content inventory, source-labelled observations, connection status, and
    reports are stored in SQLite on systems controlled by the operator. Access
    is restricted to the operator and explicitly authorized people. Google OAuth
    client credentials and refresh tokens are kept in protected secret storage
    rather than in public pages or growth reports.
  </p>

  <p>
    Operational backups may contain content metadata and aggregate observations.
    They are kept under the same restricted access controls as the active data.
    Social Agent does not currently promise a fixed retention period or
    automatic deletion schedule.
  </p>

  <h2>Revoking access and requesting deletion</h2>

  <p>
    Revoking Social Agent's Google connection stops future access after the
    authorization is no longer valid. Revocation does not by itself delete
    observations or backups already created from an earlier authorized
    connection.
  </p>

  <p>
    To ask what Google data is stored or request deletion, use the
    <a href="/about#contact">contact options on the About page</a>. The operator
    will review the active data and applicable backups and explain what can be
    removed and any operational constraints.
  </p>

  <h2>Google API policy</h2>

  <p>
    Social Agent's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs
    adheres to the
    <a
      href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a
    >, including its Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Public website analytics</h2>

  <p>
    These public information pages use the same GoatCounter pageview analytics
    as the rest of shariq.dev. That website analytics is separate from the
    Google data accessed by Social Agent.
  </p>

  <p>
    Social Agent also has an optional first-party tracker for bounded page and
    known call-to-action counts. If enabled for a site, it excludes full query
    strings and can keep validated campaign labels in same-tab
    <code>sessionStorage</code> for up to 30 minutes. The private dashboard uses authentication
    cookies. Neither feature changes the read-only Google permissions described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>

  <p>
    This notice will be updated before Social Agent uses Google user data in a
    materially different way. The date at the top identifies the current
    version.
  </p>
</SocialAgentPage>
